<title>SINGAPORE: Sri Lanka sells fuel oil to BP at minus $12.50/T.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka sells fuel oil to BP at minus $12.50/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's state-owned Ceylon Petroleum Corp (CPC) sold by tender 18,000-20,000 tonnes of fuel oil to British Petroleum at a discount of $12.50 per tonne to Singapore spot quotes, a CPC source said on Friday.</p>
<p>The 177-centistoke grade, 3.5-percent sulphur fuel oil is for May 25-26 lifting, free-on-board (fob) Colombo basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
</text>
